AirScope
Personal passive Wi-Fi / Bluetooth observation app.

Third-party data used:

1. Flock Safety / Raven / SoundThinking detection signatures (app/src/main/java/com/k/airscope/Signatures.kt)
   are derived from flock-you-esp32, fy_detect.h
   https://github.com/simeononsecurity/flock-you-esp32
   Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
   That project credits: @NitekryDPaul, DeFlockJoplin, dougborg, wgreenberg, GainSec, avenstewart,
   and colonelpanichacks/flock-you.

2. Mapped ALPR cameras and gunshot detectors are downloaded at runtime from OpenStreetMap via the
   Overpass API (tags man_made=surveillance + surveillance:type=ALPR / gunshot_detector, as used by DeFlock).
   Map data (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License (ODbL).

3. Vendor tables fetched at build time: IEEE Registration Authority MA-L registry and the
   Bluetooth SIG Assigned Numbers (company identifiers, 16-bit UUIDs).

4. Axon (Taser International) BLE prefix 00:25:DF per public research (RFParty / ABC News coverage).

Street map tiles: OpenFreeMap (https://openfreemap.org) © OpenMapTiles (https://openmaptiles.org),
data © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL).
